{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_1b32a37841f2bfc5edbf9aa70de1599ef6b3374e5906d6b3329e90fa775736bd"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Milestone completion includes starting the service in the background, smoke-testing endpoints, generating testing guides and a feedback form, and processing user feedback into fix sprints."},{"claim_ids":["clm_213f4067ea4bfbba48a888ba5b31965cbe966dfc76f319b834f9c68a6af46a83"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The framework orchestrates multiple specialized personas (orchestrator, PM, architect, engineer, UX designer, QA and support roles) working in parallel as a simulated software team."},{"claim_ids":["clm_47d1aef7cefd4e9706603fcd21591024b8bfc10141fffb6e256a3bcd612a2bde"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: contributors modify orchestrator-files/, rebuild with node build-orchestrator.js, test via ./orchestrator.sh local, and submit pull requests."},{"claim_ids":["clm_4baebc9aa6ff8d96f282a67b8f93742ba3f7fdddc2f382bf94614d82fd3290d1"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Each task produces an EVIDENCE.md with reproducible proof, complete test outputs, timestamped screenshots, and actual command execution, and validated tasks are committed with per-task file isolation."},{"claim_ids":["clm_630f464f0b624d1108fcf6f0faa481b8c64800fc24a7b7c120e4d088dcb45216"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The project is explicitly marked deprecated in favor of a new project (www.limeriq.ai), so the framework appears unmaintained at this commit."},{"claim_ids":["clm_7fd05814e743d758c61beeb11cccfbe6516a9855740f343db433509c9efc41a9"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The product's validation harness runs four parallel validators (PM end-to-end, test engineer suites and service startup, performance, security) to check milestone quality."},{"claim_ids":["clm_93d049f13402b55a31e500483d03f3f2a702be0cdffaa173d53f68406b5bea55"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Parallel execution is enforced: independent tasks must be created simultaneously in one message, with visual guides and system-level warnings against sequential execution."},{"claim_ids":["clm_9615230e83f7574c8d3104046ad3f8b80361b412f07f5d7679a6121e0aa563c6"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Installation is via an orchestrator.sh script with 'global' and 'local' modes, and global installs require explicit 'y' confirmation before overwriting, canceling on any other input."},{"claim_ids":["clm_af362b0902bcc9553983d402246be3dac275c3f7462a11418169bb5534d19ea2"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"State lives in a .work workspace organized into foundation, milestones (with per-sprint tasks, integration, numbered validation and fix-cycle directories, and completion docs), and discovery folders."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d9790da24976d619614be573fcd4fc13967075ce8a67e02a7045772eee9da5a7"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Work follows a nine-step workflow from discovery and requirements through parallel implementation, integration, validation, fix cycles, milestone completion, and feedback processing."},{"claim_ids":["clm_da456f583572300d30b967c49c2e912606c9f45278901952b625c39378f7b84d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Validation failures trigger documented fix cycles that repeat until all validators pass; the protocol treats multiple cycles as normal, honest progress."},{"claim_ids":["clm_e9fabc5d902b30151e33d340598688f80c93972d18076b92ebd97ed8ba52bce3"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The design philosophy is 'quality through truth': every claim requires evidence, failures are documented and fixed rather than hidden, which the docs say saves tokens by catching issues early."}],"claim_ids":["clm_1b32a37841f2bfc5edbf9aa70de1599ef6b3374e5906d6b3329e90fa775736bd","clm_213f4067ea4bfbba48a888ba5b31965cbe966dfc76f319b834f9c68a6af46a83","clm_47d1aef7cefd4e9706603fcd21591024b8bfc10141fffb6e256a3bcd612a2bde","clm_4baebc9aa6ff8d96f282a67b8f93742ba3f7fdddc2f382bf94614d82fd3290d1","clm_630f464f0b624d1108fcf6f0faa481b8c64800fc24a7b7c120e4d088dcb45216",